  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "A merge prints a fingerprint. We carry one forward."
    },
    {
      "t": 4.8,
      "text": "Two layers, already in the order we want."
    },
    {
      "t": 10.8,
      "text": "Merge them. Look at the middle line, that is what we keep."
    },
    {
      "t": 16.8,
      "text": "We stage it into a layer of its own. Watch the order."
    },
    {
      "t": 22.8,
      "text": "There it is, under a name of our choosing."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.8,
      "text": "A layer outside the order contributes nothing, so we add it."
    },
    {
      "t": 34.8,
      "text": "Merge again. Notice this one reports a different fingerprint."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "The file carries the earlier one, not this one's."
    },
    {
      "t": 44.8,
      "text": "Carry what the first merge printed, add it, and merge again."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that the fingerprint is only available from the merge output, that it is carried as a value, and that the second merge has a different fingerprint."
}
